              V2 cache observations use the active provider-context receipt epoch, while Responses planning retains its continuation-specific epoch and legacy initialization remains compatible.
              </?01M138G54P6DRQX9MVMY9RR64Q>
            ]>
          )>
          <Task #P2-T2 { name = "Prove atomic compaction request boundary" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 1 } (
            <Acceptance [
              <Criterion #P2-T2-AC1 { checked = true } ?01M138G54P6DRQX9MVMY9RR64R>
              The first request built from compacted history carries the successor receipt epoch, compares as epoch_boundary, and subsequent append-only requests remain same_epoch with exact prefix integrity.
              </?01M138G54P6DRQX9MVMY9RR64R>
            ]>
          )>
        ]>
      )>
      <TaskGroup #P3 { name = "Verify, install and rerun evidence" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 2 } (
        <SubNodes [
          <Task #P3-T1 { name = "Run regression, typecheck, build and local install" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 0 } (
